- `Missing required secrets: <names>. Add them to .dev.vars, .env, or set as environment variables.` at the start of `deploy`, even with `--secrets-file`. It comes from the local Wrangler session OpenNext starts to populate its cache, which reads `.dev.vars`, `.env` and the environment, never the secrets file. The upload is not affected: the file sets the secrets on the Worker. It is harmless.
- `The "middleware" file convention is deprecated. Please use "proxy" instead.` during `next dev` and `next build`. The request hook of the app is `src/middleware.ts`, not `src/proxy.ts`, on purpose: the Node.js runtime that `proxy.ts` uses is not supported by OpenNext, which runs the Edge runtime only, and `middleware.ts` compiles to it. Next.js prints the warning whenever the file exists, and no Next.js option silences it. It is harmless: keep the file. Do not migrate it to `proxy.ts`, and do not run the Next.js codemod (`@next/codemod middleware-to-proxy`): the rename breaks the Cloudflare build (`ERROR Node.js middleware is not currently supported`).
- `DeprecationWarning: Passing args to a child process with shell option true` (`DEP0190`) at the end of `deploy`, from the OpenNext CLI under a recent Node.js. It is harmless.
